      "writtenOn": "2026-08-04T08:51:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is actually already handled inside FRUTablePrint — every access is checked against table_size before we dereference. isTableEnd() stops the loop once 7 or fewer bytes are left (the up-to-3-byte pad + 4-byte CRC32 tail), so a trailing partial region never gets parsed as a record. And each field is validated before it\u0027s read: the record header, the TLV header (offsetof(value)), and the full TLV value (offset + header + length) — if anything overruns it prints a \"FRU table malformed ... out of bounds\" error and bails. So the buffer is safe to parse whatever its size; a check at the call site would just repeat these. Happy to pull one up there though if you\u0027d prefer it explicit.",
      "parentUuid": "193934bb_2f5e8fa7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 342,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 344,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "2a5f8e1431a3717e8eb7659a385ae045f5360b6c",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
